  "book.no-hunt": "No hunt available yet",  // PM_TEXT_AI
  "book.overview.body": "Type: <b>{{type}}</b>\n\nFavourite room: <b>{{room}}</b>\n\nGoal: kill every investigator before they leave.",  // PM_TEXT_AI
  "book.overview.not-yet": "chosen as the haunting begins",  // PM_TEXT_AI
  "book.overview.title": "Your ghost",  // PM_TEXT_AI
  "book.playing.body": "You are the ghost. The investigators must work out what you are and get away; you win by killing every one of them.\n\nMove with {{move}} and look with the mouse. A ghost only moves when the urge to wander comes, a few metres at a time, and when it hunts.\n\n{{journal}} opens this journal and {{pause}} its pause menu.\n\nYour favourite room is where they will look for you. When the game moves it, you have a few seconds to choose another on your map.",  // PM_TEXT_AI
  "book.playing.title": "Playing the ghost",  // PM_TEXT_AI
  "book.ready": "Ready: <b>{{interactions}}</b> interaction, <b>{{events}}</b> event, <b>{{fuses}}</b> fuse box",  // PM_TEXT_AI
  "book.ready-with-ability": "Ready: <b>{{interactions}}</b> interaction, <b>{{events}}</b> event, <b>{{abilities}}</b> ability, <b>{{fuses}}</b> fuse box",  // PM_TEXT_AI
  "book.rules.body": "Everything you do goes through the game's own rules for your type, so your evidence and behaviour stay true to it.\n\nYou can only do what your urges allow, and only when the game would let a ghost of your type do it: nothing touched before the front door opens, and a Shade keeps still while it is watched.\n\nAn interaction with an object your type rarely touches uses up more than one urge.\n\nHunts follow the game's checks: sanity, setup time, cooldown and smudging.",  // PM_TEXT_AI
